# CradleDial Architecture

- Runtime: Cloudflare Workers (TypeScript)
- Framework: Hono.js (`hono`)
- Database: Supabase PostgreSQL (`@supabase/supabase-js` initialized per-request with `SUPABASE_URL` and `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` from Worker `c.env`)
- Storage: Cloudflare R2 (`AUDIO_BUCKET` binding + `R2_PUBLIC_URL` env var)
- Telephony: Africa's Talking REST APIs (USSD, Voice, Airtime) using native Web-Standard `fetch` (DO NOT install the Node.js `africastalking` npm SDK; use clean typed `fetch` requests with `apiKey` and `Accept: application/json` headers).
- Frontend (LGA Pitch Dashboard): Single-page HTML/TailwindCSS/Vanilla JS UI served via Hono route `GET /dashboard` using official brand colors: Savannah Green (`#2E8B57`), Maternal Terracotta (`#CD5C5C`), Trust Blue (`#1E3A8A`), and Google Fonts `Nunito` and `Inter`.
- USSD Timeout Safety: All `/webhooks/ussd` responses MUST return plain text (`Content-Type: text/plain`) starting with exact `CON ` or `END ` in under 1500ms.
- Voice XML Compliance: All `/webhooks/voice/*` responses MUST return valid `application/xml`. A `<Response>` may be empty, or contain `<Play url="..."/>`, `<Say>...</Say>`, or both.
- Phone Normalization: Normalize all Nigerian phone numbers to E.164 format (`+234...`) before reading/writing to Supabase.
